I get the error when I try do do multiple cleanups with multiple test.afterAll. 

Here is a testcase that gives me the error in the ui mode with version 1.38.0 of Playwright
I think it is connected the use of page.goto in 'Cleanup: 1'

```typescript
import { test } from '@playwright/test';

test.describe.serial('Some testing', () => {
  test('A test', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('/');
  });

  test.afterAll('Cleanup: 1', async ({ browser }) => {
    const page = await browser.newPage();
    await page.goto('/');
  });

  test.afterAll('Cleanup: 2', async () => {
    // Get the error here when running. "playwright test --ui"
    // EPERM: operation not permitted, rename '...\trace.zip' -> '...\trace.zip.tmp'
    // If we remove the page.goto in "Cleanup: 1" I get no error message.
  });

  test.afterAll('Cleanup: 3', async () => {
    // Since the error dissappears quickly. I added this to be able to see the error message
    await new Promise((resolve) => { setTimeout(resolve, 20000); });
  });
});

```
